1
00:00:01,140 --> 00:00:05,120
My house in Hoang Hoa Tham is situated very deep inside the alley.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,080
Actually, it's

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:10,580
No. 17, Lane 267, Sub-lane 2

4
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:14,600
of 33 Hoang Hoa Tham Street. So if you turn down from

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:18,560
Hoang Hoa Tham Street, you have to turn about three or four times

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,780
to finally reach my house.

7
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,560
My house is located in a row of houses that is

8
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:25,020
quite secluded.

9
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:29,820
There are about six or seven houses here

10
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:33,680
sharing a common courtyard that is quite cool, with plants,

11
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:37,460
flowers, a lime tree, and jasmine.

12
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:42,030
And it's actually paved with brick,

13
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:44,720
which makes it feel very private.

14
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:48,360
Every time I enter that

15
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:50,280
secluded area,

16
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:55,160
oh, there is a sense of freshness and coolness that you can't find

17
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,400
anywhere else

18
00:00:57,280 --> 00:01:00,380
in Hanoi—at least not out on the main streets.

19
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:05,960
[laughs] My neighborhood is nested right between

20
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:09,860
three major streets: Hoang Hoa Tham to the north, Van Cao to the left,

21
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:13,760
and Doi Can to the south.

22
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:14,100
Because of this, I know about

23
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:19,120
five different ways to get to my house from those three streets, if not

24
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:22,940
more.
And this is a kind of memory that only the people

25
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:26,900
who live here know—how to navigate through the neighborhood

26
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:29,940
using those three different routes.

27
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:34,420
I know this because every time

28
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:38,060
I call ride-hailing drivers, like Grab, Be, or Xanh SM,

29
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:41,920
they usually don't know which way to go to reach my house.

30
00:01:41,980 --> 00:01:44,790
Even if they start from the main street, Hoang Hoa Tham,

31
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:48,740
they still get lost.
So I always have to give them directions on

32
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:52,740
how to navigate.
The maps aren't very accurate here;

33
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:56,620
they have to rely on the [laughs] local knowledge of the residents.

34
00:01:56,660 --> 00:02:00,480
People who have lived here for many years,

35
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:04,440
they know which path to take, which ones are blocked,

36
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,259
and where each alley leads—whether it goes out to Van Cao,

37
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:10,320
or where Van Cao connects to Doi Can Street.

38
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:15,280
The city's urban planning,

39
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:19,359
I think it will cut through from Thuy Khuê Street

40
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:22,780
to Tam Da Slope, and go straight through where my house is.

41
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:27,120
Our house will probably lose at least half, or more likely,

42
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:28,840
about eighty percent of its land.

43
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:31,920
It's fortunate that the road...

44
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:40,989
I'm quite sad because

45
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:45,060
once that road is built, people won't need to

46
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:48,500
weave through these complex alleys to find their way inside anymore.

47
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:53,080
And in general, all my memories and knowledge

48
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:56,300
about this neighborhood [laughs] won't serve any purpose anymore.

49
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,060
I feel quite sad.

50
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:03,280
Because besides being access routes, these paths are also

51
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:07,500
memories that people in this neighborhood

52
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,760
share with one another.
It creates a very strong sense of community.

53
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:15,640
Since people walk the same paths, they get to know each other.

54
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:17,580
And

55
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:22,360
there are many local vendors here, selling fish or chicken.

56
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:26,880
It's a way for families to connect.

57
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:30,700
Now, I don't know how people will interact with each other in the future,

58
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:34,620
but I'm sure we will still find things to talk about.

59
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:37,260
I moved here a very long time ago when I was a child.

60
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:38,560
Actually,

61:
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:44,220
my family moved here even before I was born.

62
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:48,680
So I've lived here since the day I came into this world. [laughs]

63
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:52,380
When I grew up a bit,

64
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:56,340
my mother would often ask me to walk to the edge of the residential area.

65
00:03:56,360 --> 00:04:00,300
Right opposite to it, there was a grocery store.

66
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:03,880
I would go there to buy beer or eggs.

67
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:07,660
Or if you turn a bit into Lane 267 Hoang Hoa Tham,

68
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:12,320
there is a spontaneous market set up by the locals.

69
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:16,680
That's the market where everyone in this Hoang Hoa Tham area

70
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:20,640
and our alley does their shopping.

71
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:21,579
It was a major source of income

72
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:26,240
for the vendors because they lived right there.

73
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:29,500
They sold everything: vegetables, meat, fish.

74
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:34,000
And everyone trusted each other.

75
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:34,320
For instance, when I went to pick up vegetables for my mom,

76
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,020
I didn't even need to pay on the spot.

77
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:40,720
I would just say, "Mom will transfer the money to you later,"

78:
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:43,280
and she would pay them later.

79
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:47,310
Because [laughs] it was like a big family, and people were happy to let you run a tab.

80
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:50,480
If you walk away from Hoang Hoa Tham towards Van Cao,

81
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:55,480
there is a very interesting spot.

82
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:59,260
This is another path that outsiders wouldn't know about.

83
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:03,240
I've never seen anyone who doesn't live here know this path.

84
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:05,780
It leads to a well.

85
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,020
That well has now been renovated

86
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:12,680
into a playground.

87
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,900
It is a cool space where people exercise.

88
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:19,600
Since it's deep in the alley, shaded by trees and surrounding buildings,

89
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:22,800
it never gets too hot.

90
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:23,440
Living here is very comfortable.

91
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:28,160
People can go there to relax, and around it,

92
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:31,360
there are some food stalls and another small spontaneous market.

93
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:36,000
Those who live [laughs] closer to the Van Cao edge do their shopping there.

94
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:36,300
Also, inside this neighborhood, there is a national relic.

95
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:39,140
This national relic will likely end up on the main street,

96
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,440
or very close to it.

97
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:49,020
It's a pagoda—I don't remember the name,

98:
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:51,180
but you can look it up. It's located in Lane 267 Hoang Hoa Tham.

99
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:55,240
Also, this area is...

100
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:58,360
It has become quite youthful now with many new coffee shops.

101
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:05,900
So many coffee shops and eateries.

102
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:08,460
Not just traditional Vietnamese spots, but even ramen shops,

103
00:06:09,180 --> 00:06:12,680
and all kinds of cafes: garden cafes, study cafes.

104
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:16,480
But the most famous ones here are probably the garden cafes.

105
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:18,640
Again, because this area is very green,

106
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:22,140
though these green spaces will likely disappear in the future.

107
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:27,360
When they clear the land to build the road,

108
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:31,100
those shops will be replaced by the road, and all the trees will be cut down.

109
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:35,340
I feel very sorry because

110
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:38,240
these "third spaces" and cooling areas

111
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:42,320
are already extremely rare in the city.

112
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:45,220
Once this neighborhood is demolished, we will lose even more of them.

113
00:06:45,270 --> 00:06:45,370
[background music]
